{
  "name": "WASL Saudi-dialect check-in answers",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Synthetic, hand-written answers in the style of Saudi patients and family members replying to WASL check-in questions. Not real patients. Written before the parser existed. Labels describe what the speaker means, not what any parser can detect.",
  "questions": {
    "MED_START": "بديت الدواء الجديد <دواء>؟",
    "MED_CONTINUE": "للحين مستمر على <دواء>؟",
    "STOPPED_CHECK": "وقّفت <دواء> زي ما قال لك الدكتور؟",
    "DOSE_CHECK": "تاخذ <دواء> على الجرعة الجديدة اللي في ورقة الخروج؟",
    "OPEN_MEDS": "فيه أي دواء ثاني تاخذه ما ذكرناه؟"
  },
  "labellingRules": [
    "expectedIntent = what the speaker means as an answer to the question exactly as worded above.",
    "Hedged answers (اظن، يمكن، مو متأكد) are UNSURE even when they lean yes or no — except OPEN_MEDS, where any medicine mention is MENTIONS_MEDS (a mention must reach a clinician).",
    "Partial adherence (مو كل يوم، ساعات اخذها وساعات لا) to a \"still taking / started?\" question is NO.",
    "\"Yes, but I forgot yesterday\" to a start/continue question is YES (the medicine was started / is being continued).",
    "STOPPED_CHECK: a yes to \"did you stop?\" is STOPPED; a no, or still taking, is STILL_TAKING.",
    "DOSE_CHECK: a yes to \"on the new dose?\" is NEW_DOSE; a no, or still on the previous dose, is OLD_DOSE.",
    "UNKNOWN = the reply does not answer the question (off-topic, filler, a question back).",
    "expectedMeds = drug ids the text names unambiguously (generic, brand, or an informal name that refers to exactly one drug in the demo dictionary). Shared informal names (حبة الضغط، حبة السيولة، حبوب المعدة، حبوب السكر، المسكن) and herbs are not listed.",
    "tags: \"hard\" marks items a human would still find tricky or that need knowledge beyond the words (numbers, brands, buried intent)."
  ],
